## Role 7 — Department Head (`Department Head`)

### Responsibilities
- Submit Store Requisitions on behalf of their unit  
- **First-level approve or reject** requisitions and returns submitted by their own staff (before PAO)  
- Submit Material Return Requests (SRN) for items no longer needed or defective  
- Initiate Material Transfer Requests to/from their unit's store  
- View stock and fixed-asset records relevant to their unit, including staff User-Cards  

### Sidebar — `DEPT_HEAD_NAV` (label: **Department & Unit Operations**)
| Section | Items |
|---|---|
| Overview | Department Dashboard (`/`) |
| Unit Requisitions & Approvals | Submit Store Requisition (`/requisitions`), Approve/Reject Staff Requisitions (`/requisitions`), Approve/Reject Staff Returns (`/returns`) |
| Returns & Transfers | Submit Material Return (SRN) (`/returns`), Initiate Inter-Unit Transfer (`/transfers`) |
| Unit Property View | Stock Overview (Read-Only) (`/stock-cards`), Fixed Assets & User-Cards (Unit View) (`/fixed-assets`), Item Catalog (`/items`) |

### Department Head Dashboard
- **Stat cards**: My unit's pending requisitions, staff returns awaiting my decision, pending transfers, fixed assets under unit custody
- **Live Worklist — "Staff Requisitions Awaiting My Approval"**: lists `requisitions` with `status === "Pending Approval"` for their department. Each row has **Approve / Reject** 1-click actions (calls `decideRequisition`).
- **Live Worklist — "Staff Returns Awaiting My Review"**: lists `returns` with `status === "Pending Approval"` for their department. **Approve / Reject** 1-click actions (calls `decideReturn`).
- **Quick Actions**: New Requisition, Submit Return, Initiate Transfer, View Fixed Assets.
- **Unit Fixed-Asset Summary**: shows assets whose `department` matches the Dept Head's unit.

### Permission Changes in Workflow Pages

#### `Requisitions.jsx`
- `canRequest` already includes `"Department Head"` ✓  
- `canApprove` already includes `"Department Head"` ✓  

#### `Returns.jsx`
- `canRequest` currently only includes `"Department Head"` — verify this is correct ✓  

#### `Transfers.jsx`
- Add `"Department Head"` to `canInitiate` so they can submit transfer requests.

